# MadGraph5 batch script: u d > e+ e- u d at QCD=0, fixed scale, partonic beams.
#
# The multi-rung t-channel reference: the one banked run whose diagrams carry a
# genuine ladder of spacelike lines, so a phase-space map that orders its rungs
# wrongly has something to disagree with.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - Its 35 diagrams split 12 / 14 / 9 over one, two and three spacelike lines.
#     Every rung count the ordered-chain decomposition has to handle is present in
#     one subprocess, and the two- and three-rung diagrams are the majority. The
#     three-rung ones are the multiperipheral topology where the e+ and the e-
#     leave the chain at *different* vertices across a spacelike lepton line — the
#     case where an ordering is least like a relabelling.
#   - The rungs are asymmetric: the blobs a chain emits are a single jet, a single
#     lepton and a lepton pair, and the spacelike poles are a mix of massless
#     (photon, quark, lepton) and m_Z lines. A chain whose rungs were
#     interchangeable would make any ordering test vacuous; these are not.
#   - QCD=0 keeps the diagram set to the electroweak ladders and removes the
#     strong coupling entirely, so nothing here waits on the kT clustering: with
#     no alpha_s in the matrix element and no PDF on either beam, the scale
#     prescription cannot reach the cross section at all.
#
# Why partonic (lpp = 0) rather than `p p > e+ e- j j QCD=0`:
#   The hadronic spelling of the same physics decomposes into 112 non-empty
#   subprocesses and 3024 diagrams, which this crate's flavour grouping turns into
#   60 groups pooling 1608 sampling channels. A multichannel evaluates every
#   channel's density at every point, so that is some sixty times the per-point
#   cost of the pp_to_llj_fixed row (24 channels) on a final state needing more
#   points, and MadGraph would have to integrate and store all 112 subprocesses.
#   The one concrete flavour assignment carries the whole ladder spectrum at 35
#   channels, which is what the reference exists to exercise. The flavour union
#   and the (tau, y) convolution are already gated by the Drell-Yan and llj rows,
#   so nothing is lost by fixing the initial state here.
#
# The run card follows the partonic precedent (uux_to_epemg) plus the fixed-scale
# and LHAPDF lines of pp_to_llj_fixed:
#
#   - lpp1 = lpp2 = 0 with ebeam 250 each, so `launch` integrates sigma-hat at a
#     fixed 500 GeV and the cross section is comparable point for point with this
#     crate's fixed-beam path.
#   - fixed_ren_scale / fixed_fac_scale1 / fixed_fac_scale2 = True at m_Z. With
#     QCD=0 and no PDF none of the three can move the answer; they are set so the
#     claim that this row is scale-independent is literal rather than inferred.
#   - mmll = 50, for the reason pp_to_llj_fixed gives: it holds the run out of the
#     low-m_ll region where the Drell-Yan comparison carries a standing
#     few-percent discrepancy, so a cross section gated here does not inherit it.
#   - use_syst False, as every other lpp = 0 run: the reweighting bookkeeping has
#     no consumer on a partonic row.
#
# Everything else (ptj 20, ptl 10, etaj 5, etal 2.5, drll = drjl = 0.4) is left at
# the defaults the llj cards use. ptj 20 is load-bearing twice over: it regulates
# the t-channel singularity that would otherwise dominate sigma-hat, and it is the
# scale the peripheral channels bound their momentum transfer by.
generate u d > e+ e- u d QCD=0
output ud_to_epemud_qcd0 -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set fixed_ren_scale True
set fixed_fac_scale1 True
set fixed_fac_scale2 True
set scale 91.188
set dsqrt_q2fact1 91.188
set dsqrt_q2fact2 91.188
set mmll 50
set use_syst False
done
